<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wars of Castro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1641">1641</a>–<a href="/years/1649">1649</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Wars of Castro were two conflicts over the Duchy of Castro, a Farnese fief in the Papal States north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. In the first, from 1641 to 1644, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-urban-viii">Pope Urban VIII</a> fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoardo-farnese-duke-of-parma">Odoardo Farnese, Duke of Parma</a>, who was backed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, Tuscany and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modena">Modena</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a> was forced to make peace. In the second, in 1649, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-x">Pope Innocent X</a> captured and razed the town of Castro.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wars-of-castro.jpg" alt="Wars of Castro" width="320" height="236" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joan Blaeu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joan_Blaeu_-_Theatrum_civitatum_et_admirandorum_Italiae_-_page_371_Castro_21_(crop).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
